        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Capture cards from table layout. First player/team to reach 21 points wins, with special endgame rules.',
          gameplay: "Play counter-clockwise. Must play exactly one card per turn. Three possible uses: Capture (captura/cojer) - take matching card(s) or builds; Build (forma) - combine with table cards into single build (sum=value) or multiple build (sets with same value); Trail - leave card on table. Restrictions: Build owner must hold matching card; Build owner cannot trail (must capture or build more); Cannot trail if played card matches any loose table card (must capture or build); Can capture builds only by matching value; Can increase single build value by adding card (become new owner). Cannot build for partner in partnership game. Cards left capturable called 'dejado' (left) or 'pisado' (stepped). Sweep: clear all table cards (scores bonus).",
          keyRules: [
            'Counter-clockwise play and deal',
            'Card values: K=13, Q=12, J=11, A=1 or 14',
            'Must play exactly one card per turn',
            'Capture matching cards or builds',
            'Build: single (sum) or multiple (sets with same value)',
            'Build owner must hold matching card',
            'Build owner cannot trail',
            'Cannot trail if card matches loose table card',
            'Cannot build for partner',
            'Can increase single build value (take ownership)',
            'Sweep: clear table = 1 point',
            'Game to 21 with special endgame at 18+',
            'Ties score nothing for that category',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Capture cards when possible. Build when you have strong capturing cards. Avoid leaving sweeps for opponents.',
          intermediate: "Track which cards have been played. Use building to secure future captures. Time your sweeps carefully. In partnership game, coordinate with partner's builds.",
          advanced: 'Complex building strategies to deny opponents captures. Force opponents to leave dejado/pisado cards. Endgame strategy when nearing 21: focus on sweeps and guaranteed points (aces, casinos) rather than most cards/spades. Use drifting (intentional non-capture) strategically.',
          tips: [
            'Ace is very powerful (value 14) - use wisely',
            'Building high values (13-14) is strong but risky',
            "Don't trail when you match a loose card",
            'Watch for sweep opportunities',
            'In endgame (18+ points), sweeps become crucial',
            "Partners: don't steal partner's builds",
            'Track spades for the spade bonus',
            '10â™¦ and 2â™  are valuable - prioritize capturing them',
